("what's the meaning of life",
"""There may not be a single meaning handed to us, and many thinkers, from Epicurus to the existentialists, have argued that this is less a tragedy than an invitation. If meaning isn't given, it has to be made, and people make it in remarkably consistent ways: through love and friendship, through work that matters to someone, through curiosity and beauty, through being useful to others, and through a sense of belonging to something larger than themselves. If you want a short answer, I'd offer this one: to pay close attention to the world, and to leave some part of it kinder than you found it. Douglas Adams, of course, suggested forty-two."""),

